  "question": "Do these finite numeric initial index candidates match independently DAO-created controls in exact saved scalar bits, full metadata, rows, raw keys/locators/maps/counts, directed traversal, Seek and isolated rejection probes?",
  "sequence": [
    "Commit and independently review this pinned plan before one DAO dispatch. The deterministic Rust exporter calls the public creation API once per arm; eight external immutable candidate identities bind the reviewed source.",
    "For eight arms and three replicas each, copy the pinned candidate and create a fresh matching DAO control with the frozen EXP0171 dedicated type setters, including its local Decimal Currency setter. Close all objects, then capture candidate/control read-only.",
    "For each role create a separate duplicate-probe copy and require DAO3022; the required mixed arm also gets a separate null-probe copy requiring DAO3058. Cancel rejected updates, close, capture complete logical and raw state. Baseline originals remain untouched.",
    "Retain102 MDBs/102 complete unchanged read-only observations:48 baselines,48 duplicate copies,6 required-null copies. Unexpected errors stop once with initiating endpoint/stack and retention failures. No automatic retry or subset promotion."
  ],
  "decision_rule": "All24 pairs,102 identities and complete captures/probes must pass. Full schemas/field/index properties, exact hex/Boolean rows, complete directed traversal and declared full-key non-null Seek results are mandatory. Equal-key traversal ties alone may reorder; complete rows remain checked. Both roles raw keys/locators/distinct counts/tree graph/maps must match the independent finite transforms and requested rows. Physical page numbers/layout/compression need not equal across roles. All rejection copies retain the requested complete baseline state. Otherwise no_outcome.",
  "bounds": "Eight finite arms cover new Boolean/Byte/Integer/Currency/Single/Double types with selected directions, Double IgnoreAllNull, mixed Currency/Double nullable Include and required Integer/Single. Mixed Include126rows crosses the public22byte-entry leaf boundary. Other arms2..9rows; no arbitrary Cartesian type/direction/policy claim. Private catalog MAX_ROWS_PER_PAGE256 and existing64page bound; pure EXP0146 tree decoder permits observed branch markers1/2. No BooleanNull/negativezero/nonfinite/Date/Binary/Text/GUID/LVAL keys. Non-Long null/composite transforms are explicit candidate hypotheses, not inferred universal DAO rules. One SSH job<=600seconds. Local development only; no support movement."
}
